== Recent News

- \[November 2024\] 3 papers presented at [https://www.corl.org/ CoRL 2024]: [https://skillgen.github.io/ SkillMimicGen] (a data generation system that is a subtantial improvement over [https://mimicgen.github.io/ MimicGen]), [https://sites.google.com/view/spire-corl-2024 SPIRE] (a framework that combines RL, imitation, and planning to solve long-horizon tasks), and [https://nodtamp.github.io/ NOD-TAMP] (a system for solving long-horizon tasks from a few human demos).

- \[October 2024\] New preprints on [https://aha-vlm.github.io/ AHA] (novel failure data generation and failure reasoning framework for robotic manipulation) and [https://latentactionpretraining.github.io/ LAPA] (unsupervised latent action based pretraining for robotic manipulation).

- \[July 2024\] We released the full [https://github.com/NVlabs/mimicgen MimicGen data generation code]! Easily generate large-scale robot demonstrations from just a few human demonstrations.

== About Me

I am a research scientist at NVIDIA AI. I obtained my PhD degree from Stanford University, co-advised by [http://cvgl.stanford.edu/silvio/ Silvio Savarese] and [http://vision.stanford.edu/feifeili/ Fei-Fei Li]. My research focuses on developing systems and algorithms to enable robots to learn useful manipulation tasks.

